Tullius, the second son of an earl''s family, died in modern-day Japan and was reincarnated as a child in a fantasy world ruled by swords and magic. His only wish is simple: "I never want to die again." Having experienced the terror of death once, he is even more afraid of dying than most. He refuses to accept dying from old age, illness, or being killed by others.

Driven by this obsession, he clings to alchemy, a form of magic that is said to grant immortality when perfected. However, alchemy is considered a mere exaggerated myth by the rest of the world. Furthermore, Tullius'' alchemy research takes a disturbing turn. Brainwashing, modification, human dissection... His repeated, abnormal experiments make him feared and reviled by those around him, but he doesn''t care at all. One day, Tullius receives a strange order from his brother, who should have hated him—what will happen next?

(Source: Shufu no Tomo-sha, translated)');

Jun is a fifteen-year-old boy living in an elegant mansion. He has a teacher to give him lessons at home, and he studies the violin. He never leaves his home, though, due to his severe congenital heart disease. When any overexertion might lead to his death, playing it safe has always taken priority over interacting with other people.

Jun and Ai, both feeling confined and lonely, find each other through an internet social network on their cell phones. Soon, they have formed a deep friendship and possibly more. But will their affection for each other be able to overcome the extreme differences in their lives and upbringing?

(Source: MangaHelpers)');
