One night, Giselle stumbles upon the dark secret of Rose Hill: a black-haired boy with piercing yellow eyes, whose true form is revealed from drinking her blood—a handsome vampire who has been imprisoned and starved for years by Carter''s family. Giselle is moved by his sorrowful eyes, and she cannot help but believe that she has found a kindred soul. But pursuing that connection only leads her down a path of forbidden love, carnal lust, and deep thirst for blood.');

Samatoki is tasked with eliminating the drug dealers who have moved in onto his gang''s turf. He finds that his fellow teammate, Jyuto Iruma, is also investigating Grasshopper for the police, and the two decide to team up to find the origins of the substance.

Meanwhile, a friend of Jirou Yamada seeks Ichirou''s help in tracking down the whereabouts of his younger brother, who was kidnapped by a rival gang and is being held for ransom. Unable to go to the police for assistance, the Yamada brothers take the matter into their own hands. The youngest brother, Saburou, immediately suspects that something is amiss about Jirou''s friend, but Ichirou cannot abandon someone in need.

As the two teams delve further into their separate investigations, they encounter old friends and enemies. With an unknown culprit pulling the strings, Ichirou and Samatoki will stop at nothing to figure out who is responsible.');

Elsewhere, a young kid approaches Doppo Kannonzaka on his way home from work, insisting that he take them to go see Jakurai. The kid''s older brother was abducted by a Yokohama gang, and they are demanding a ransom. Informing him of the urgent news, Jakurai, with Doppo and Hifumi Izanami at his side, sets out to confront the gang in the middle of the night.

When the two teams arrive at the scene, they find old friends and enemies awaiting them. Sensing that there is someone behind the incidents, Ramuda and Jakurai are more determined than ever to uncover the truth.');

