"Your one duty is this: to be by my side when I sleep. However, you must remain awake. If it becomes too much to bear, you may cut me down. I will not hold it against you."

Leaving those cryptic words behind, he falls asleep, and Amarion realizes why the Grand Duke sought out a knight specifically to take as his wife. As her nights of sleepless vigilance stretch on, his attitude toward her grows sweeter and sweeter—until at last, Death smiles at her with breathtaking warmth and calls out:

"My lady, will you allow me to call you by your name?"

