But the man who shows up is the last person Hyeokjun ever expected, Choi Jeongheon, the ex who ghosted him four years ago and left him shattered.

Hyeokjun is furious. If his father will not fire Jeongheon, then he will drive him out himself. He throws tantrums, picks fights, and schemes nonstop, but Jeongheon remains calm, unbothered, and frustratingly professional.

Digging through memories of their breakup, Hyeokjun finally stumbles upon the perfect plan for revenge.

"I found it. The way to completely ruin Choi Jeongheon...!"

But as he launches his little war, the line between torment and attraction begins to blur, and Hyeokjun discovers that the one person he wants to destroy might also be the one he still cannot let go.

(Source: Lezhin Entertainment)');

"I like the name Shigure."

"I prefer being alone and don''t want to deal with unnecessary people... but if it''s you, Shigure, I don''t mind."

Junna, who only appears on damp, rainy days, is expressionless and dry in demeanor, yet oddly close in proximity and eager for affection. Then, on a sunny day, Shigure discovers Junna''s "secret"—and from that moment, the distance between them shrinks to the point where he can feel her breath. Her overwhelming affection begins to spill out uncontrollably...

(Source: Kadokawa, translated)');

