Kai, a high school girl, encounters a couple who have broken up over a trivial matter at her part-time job. Just as she was thinking that she wanted to be careful and cherish her own love life, she unexpectedly reunites with Azuma, who had been dumped, at a committee meeting!? While feeling uneasy around Azuma, she is flustered by his help, and then she encounters him again when he is being dumped by yet another girl...!?

(Source: Kodansha, translated)');

(Source: MANGA Plus)');

Elle was loved by all the knights and lived a life full of happiness... or so it seemed... but then, memories of her past life running a small restaurant came flooding back to her, and she realized there was one huge problem...! "The food in this country is absolutely terrible...!" To make delicious food in this remote land, Elle decides to become the Knight Order''s cook...! And when everyone tastes her cooking, it receives nothing but enormous praise...!?

Armed with knowledge from her past life and the blessings of the spirits, she works hard on the frontier! An adored little girl''s isekai culinary fantasy!

(Source: Starts Shuupan, translated)');

(Source: MANGA Plus)');
CREATE TABLE manga_author(
                author_id INTEGER REFERENCES author(author_id),
                manga_id INTEGER REFERENCES manga(manga_id),

                PRIMARY KEY (author_id, manga_id)
            );
CREATE TABLE manga_genres(
                manga_id INTEGER REFERENCES manga(manga_id),
                genre_id INTEGER REFERENCES genres(genre_id),

                PRIMARY KEY (manga_id, genre_id)
            );
CREATE TABLE pending_recovery(username TEXT PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE relationships(
                user_id_left INTEGER REFERENCES users(user_id),
                user_id_right INTEGER REFERENCES users(user_id),
                created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,

                CONSTRAINT chk_numerical_order CHECK (user_id_left < user_id_right),
                PRIMARY KEY (user_id_left, user_id_right)
            );
CREATE TABLE users(
                user_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
                username TEXT NOT NULL,
                gender TEXT,
                birthday INTEGER,
                location TEXT,
                entries INTEGER,
                scraped_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,

                UNIQUE(username)
            );
CREATE INDEX usern_id_entries ON entries (user_id);
CREATE INDEX manga_id_entries ON entries (manga_id);
CREATE INDEX manga_id_genre ON manga_genres (manga_id);
CREATE INDEX genre_id_manga ON manga_genres (genre_id);
COMMIT;
